#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275593 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "783ca59b-0242-584c-ae47-004a0eb03817" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Left or Right-Opening Parabola Given the Vertex and Another Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b544aef-4b08-566e-b89f-6375a971585d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=\\frac{9}{5}(x-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275595} {:answer/id #uuid "4c76720f-5fc0-51b7-81e1-07a6b885a8a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y+2)^{2}=\\frac{9}{20}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275596} {:answer/id #uuid "aed3fca7-d8d1-57a1-b538-8ed46c92bfa6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}=\\frac{9}{5}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275597} {:answer/id #uuid "b019f271-7470-5ee4-bd93-d25a46cebb3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}=\\frac{9}{20}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275598} {:answer/id #uuid "024188a7-1314-5685-a589-3841147df8e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y-2)^{2}=\\frac{9}{5}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275599}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "024188a7-1314-5685-a589-3841147df8e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y-2)^{2}=\\frac{9}{5}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275599} :answer-field/id #uuid "f922b8c4-d133-5566-9064-c0537c542bff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275594}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0695a7e0-e42c-5754-8590-aebc60ec68a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-115648" :question/problem "Find the equation of the right-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(0,2)$ and passes through the point $(5,5).$" :question/worked-solution "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(0,2),$ we substitute $h=0$ and $k=2$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =4px.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(5,5),$ so we can substitute $x=5$ and $y=5$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =4px \\\\ (5-2)^{2} & =4p(5) \\\\ 9 & =20p \\\\ p & =\\frac{9}{20}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =4px \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =4(\\frac{9}{20})x \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =\\frac{9}{5}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275600 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "17099881-d7b9-54d9-a29a-4f5f28561cd3" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Left or Right-Opening Parabola with Vertex at the Origin Given Another Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f6c6b385-6262-53cd-b0cd-1339614594ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=9x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275602} {:answer/id #uuid "162da332-aa1f-514d-911d-329c1bec9a4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275603} {:answer/id #uuid "e0afeb06-eb2c-55c1-a731-fbf163e39787" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=6x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275604} {:answer/id #uuid "915837fd-2465-5bc4-ae59-dc897eb18047" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-6x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275605} {:answer/id #uuid "2df3aa65-f295-50e6-9f8e-9bf258a81fbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-9x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275606}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2df3aa65-f295-50e6-9f8e-9bf258a81fbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-9x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275606} :answer-field/id #uuid "2df90e78-eaad-52d7-8f65-be2a782aab58" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275601}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4efb81e2-31d7-5984-8b91-b81d7384111a" :question/math-academy-id "q-11767" :question/problem "Find the equation of the left-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(-4,-6).$" :question/worked-solution "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(-4,-6),$ we can substitute $x=-4$ and $y=-6$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ (-6)^{2} & =4p(-4) \\\\ 36 & =-16p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{9}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(-\\frac{9}{4})x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-9x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275607 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "17099881-d7b9-54d9-a29a-4f5f28561cd3" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Left or Right-Opening Parabola with Vertex at the Origin Given Another Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d568472-481f-54ca-9b7d-15fc01cd1025" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275609} {:answer/id #uuid "b586c5e3-ef3f-5fed-a09a-a80833331276" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=7x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275610} {:answer/id #uuid "f1df571b-393c-532b-bf2a-0e654295747a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-7x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275611} {:answer/id #uuid "ae4a04d3-f737-5f67-a709-217ce6beca1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275612} {:answer/id #uuid "8e08d898-3712-565e-b519-254dbd30f472" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275613}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1df571b-393c-532b-bf2a-0e654295747a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-7x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275611} :answer-field/id #uuid "13c83e8b-3fac-5c55-b695-63be4c782c7c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275608}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9f5d2d16-f7ab-5a64-837e-def4991cf53a" :question/math-academy-id "q-11772" :question/problem "Find the equation of the left-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(-7,-7).$" :question/worked-solution "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(-7,-7),$ we can substitute $x=-7$ and $y=-7$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ (-7)^{2} & =4p(-7) \\\\ 49 & =-28p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{7}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(-\\frac{7}{4})x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-7x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275614 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc86c375-c2c4-56b7-a207-0abfc9709f6a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Left or Right-Opening Parabola Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b922c2d3-d768-5e43-8ba7-8372b7d2df11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y-4)^{2}=-\\frac{16}{3}(x-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275616} {:answer/id #uuid "ec9f01bf-aa36-51b4-9cdf-ffecaf5162b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y-2)^{2}=-\\frac{16}{3}(x-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275617} {:answer/id #uuid "e0e8ff05-b7ec-5e45-a2d1-669cc182b0e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y-2)^{2}=\\frac{16}{3}(x-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275618} {:answer/id #uuid "29ea01b8-0aa6-5d35-a52d-9bcb70fa3273" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y-2)^{2}=-\\frac{8}{3}(x-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275619} {:answer/id #uuid "535a72ef-50fb-52d3-ab41-bd3c2fc45b39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y-2)^{2}=\\frac{8}{3}(x-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275620}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec9f01bf-aa36-51b4-9cdf-ffecaf5162b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y-2)^{2}=-\\frac{16}{3}(x-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275617} :answer-field/id #uuid "bca9c68d-9188-5543-b70a-8309a1436c55" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275615}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "414e12b5-a489-588c-a563-174560530b26" :question/math-academy-id "q-11807" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972835/assets/e4b681e9bdf5fa8021ca359e0bf93c27b53a18f0d5e906765a911a72ecfc0159.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram we see that the arms of the parabola open to the left. The parabola has its vertex at $(4,2)$ and passes through the point $(-8,10).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(4,2),$ we substitute $h=4$ and $k=2$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =4p(x-4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(-8,10),$ so we can substitute $x=-8$ and $y=10$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =4p(x-4) \\\\ (10-2)^{2} & =4p(-8-4) \\\\ 64 & =-48p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =4p(x-4) \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =4(-\\frac{4}{3})(x-4) \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =-\\frac{16}{3}(x-4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the left since $p=-\\frac{4}{3}$ is negative."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275621 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc86c375-c2c4-56b7-a207-0abfc9709f6a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Left or Right-Opening Parabola Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5bc2757-af02-5fdd-9bc3-bf441e418da1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y-4)^{2}=5(x-6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275623} {:answer/id #uuid "f7dd7722-90da-5c97-a13a-dfbbd066e68e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y-4)^{2}=-5(x-6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275624} {:answer/id #uuid "0e05bdfc-5427-5883-b1a1-c0528d15dc1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y-4)^{2}=3(x-6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275625} {:answer/id #uuid "bea63f44-af12-5db3-9c3f-7cc44ca93e99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y-4)^{2}=-3(x-6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275626} {:answer/id #uuid "6cf93320-bffb-5854-88c9-1f611ce453a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y-6)^{2}=-5(x-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275627}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7dd7722-90da-5c97-a13a-dfbbd066e68e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y-4)^{2}=-5(x-6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275624} :answer-field/id #uuid "48ac1084-7cac-57fd-a633-8484341c8cfa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275622}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "55ed2b91-76f2-5ba6-93e2-258601e00a25" :question/math-academy-id "q-11811" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972835/assets/ecf128d341a8a568ade4abaa2a59e1083d2c436fdb3d2a0b4b642fb7e85cee63.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram we see that the arms of the parabola open to the left. The parabola has its vertex at $(6,4)$ and passes through the point $(1,9).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(6,4),$ we substitute $h=6$ and $k=4$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-4)^{2} & =4p(x-6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(1,9),$ so we can substitute $x=1$ and $y=9$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-4)^{2} & =4p(x-6) \\\\ (9-4)^{2} & =4p(1-6) \\\\ 25 & =-20p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-4)^{2} & =4p(x-6) \\\\ (y-4)^{2} & =4(-\\frac{5}{4})(x-6) \\\\ (y-4)^{2} & =-5(x-6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the left since $p=-\\frac{5}{4}$ is negative."}]}
